Hello, gentlemen.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:20.560
Can you hear me?

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.120
Yeah.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:22.160
All right.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.680
I put the summary over there in the Google chat.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.080
For those of you who are curious, read it.

00:02:54.969 --> 00:02:56.010
Is Thomas on?

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.450
Is George on the call?

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:00.840
Yeah, you're all there.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.960
Awesome.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.439
All right.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.110
So.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.500
Shall we begin?

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.300
Yes.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:13.780
Yeah.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:21.780
The party stood at the threshold of a ruined reception hall, its walls are adorned with faded murals depicting grand welcomes that had long since turned to ruin.

00:03:21.939 --> 00:03:32.820
Battered furniture lined the walls, skeletons of humans and other humanoids lay scattered across the floor, and at the center of the room sat what appeared to be a filth-covered, decorative statue of a Minotaur upon a throne.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.700
No torches remained in the many crescents and wall scones.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.780
The only light was with a party carried in with him.

00:03:37.939 --> 00:03:39.540
It was Sequioa who noticed first.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.420
The creature was not stone at all, but very much alive.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.540
He quietly pulled the door shut before it could spot them, and the party huddled together to decide their next move.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:55.939
The Minotaur spoke only Abyssal, a language none of them knew, not even Vurakal, the fire salamander, who complicated any plan to talk their way through.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.300
Rather than cut the beast down, the group chose a bolder gambit.

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:03.300
They would walk in with Calmer dressed as the Earth Cleric and Zephyr announcing, We're your boss.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:10.740
The Minotaur, it turned out, harbored a deep and violent hatred for the temple's former leadership, and the announcement sent it into a rage.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:17.780
I charged Zephyr with terrifying speed, goring him savagely for 17 points of damage and hurling to the ground.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.660
Zephyr rolled a natural run on the strength shade.

00:04:22.259 --> 00:04:28.660
Before looming over him with a murderous intemp, the double-headed axe in hand, Zinnia moved to strike the creature, but failed to land a blow.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:40.340
And it was Calmer who stepped forward with a calm and persuasive voice, rolling a 21 on persuasion and somehow managing to give the beast pause, though it pointedly gestured at the prone Zephyr as if sizing up eating material.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.340
Zephyr, battered and prone on the cold stone floor, pleaded, We are different.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:49.780
Then offered the creature food from the party's packs, and the monitor, grumbling and suspicious, began to eat.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.700
With its hunger momentarily satisfied, the creature girt to terms.

00:04:53.939 --> 00:05:02.819
It grumbled of bandits, men's in black coats who had come and attacked it, and it would guard the reception hall in exchange for regular food and protection from them.

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:04.500
Well, this is not my room.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:09.860
I stand guard, it declared, as long as the food keeps coming, and no more bandit come and back and attack.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:15.620
Then it turned its gaze back to Zephyr and said with a surprising casualness, No hard feelings.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.379
The truce came with a pointed warning.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.460
However, if bandit come attack, I find you, I kill you, I eat you.

00:05:21.779 --> 00:05:22.660
Zephyr promised.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:37.700
The party accepted the arrangement and quietly noted they now had a very large, very hungry guard on their payroll, and Zephyr had to physically pull Calmer aside to stop the cleric from demanding the minotaur formally acknowledge a new clerical order with the high lord Master Calmer.

00:05:38.259 --> 00:05:43.540
As the group moved deeper into the temple's corner doors, Calmer began to reveal a troubling shift in his thinking.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:51.300
When the subject of feeding the monitor arose again, he calmly suggested that four prisoners still held captives somewhere in the temple could solve the problem neatly.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.820
Two birds, one stone.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.860
Don't forget, he reminded, we are now the evil overlords of this temple.

00:05:56.019 --> 00:05:58.820
Freeing good people is not exactly something we should be doing.

00:05:59.139 --> 00:06:06.019
When Sequioa asked whether he was trying to get his clerical abilities taken away, Calmer airily explained that this was a common misconception.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:10.019
That once a cleric reaches a certain level of power, that power is intrinsic to him.

00:06:10.259 --> 00:06:17.220
Even Frostband, the party's sentient sword, chimed to remind Sequioa that their plan had always been to remain discreet and avoid drawing attention to themselves.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:21.940
Calmer, for his first part, reflected openly on his disillusionment with the Church of St.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:22.660
Cuthbert.

00:06:22.899 --> 00:06:29.620
His companions had arranged his return with Zinnia surrendering a magical trident to Turjon as payment.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.820
Loyalty is a two-way street, he said, and you have demonstrated loyalty, and I will demonstrate loyalty to you.

00:06:35.139 --> 00:06:35.540
As for St.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:38.340
Cuthbert and I, we have a good working relationship.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:44.980
He was not yet an evil man, he insisted, but the reading material did put a different perspective on the endless prattle of St.

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:51.700
Cuthbert, and he had been scribbling notes about a potential new educational system inspired by the principles of the Earth Temple.

00:06:52.019 --> 00:06:57.060
The party pressed on, discovering a series of storerooms that revealed just how well supplied the temple truly was.

00:06:57.379 --> 00:07:12.259
One room held stacks of lumber and firewood, while a second, its lock, no match for Sequioa's skills and a hard roll of 33, contained a remarkable cache of equipment, chain mail, plate armor, backpacks, holy water, lanterns, lockpicks, mirrors, parchments, ropes, sacks, spikes, and tinder boxes.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.019
Zephyr, as chief of operations, resolved to get well to delegate.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.460
We'll get some other guys to do this.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:21.060
Calmer surveyed the rotting remains of what had once been a food storage area.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:27.510
The mess absolutely unacceptable, and suggested that Dren Halveth and the broken blades be brought to clean it up.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:31.750
Zephyr agreed that Dren was fond of Manuel Lambert.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:48.950
He then proposed assigning an individual storeroom to each of the elemental temples, accidentally counting the water temple twice, prompting Sequioa to needle him that somebody didn't pass school, before pulling out a scrap of scroll to begin making notes on a chaotic Earth Temple educational system before anyone could stop him.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:57.590
The exploration was cut short when a massive, demented ghoul lurched out of the shadows of a corridor and fixed its hollow gaze on living warp of the party.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:08.950
Zinnia immediately recognized immediately that a necromancer had been at work, the same one responsible for the undead that had plagued the temple before, now raising far more dangerous creatures than before.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.070
The battle was brutal.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:14.870
Sequioa struck first from hiding for 29 points of damage, and Zephyr followed with his pistol.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:19.910
The first shot, a natural one, his second landing for roughly 31 points with his assassin's bonus.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:25.270
The ghoul sank its teeth into Calmer for 21 points of damage, and the cleric crumpled, paralyzed by the bite.

00:08:25.509 --> 00:08:29.190
Sequioa took eight points from its claws, but shrugged off the paralysis.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:41.750
Zinnia rolled a natural 20 to rather the creature's foul, poisonous stench, having, as the masked by, smelled and tasted worse than his life, and delivered a series of devastating blows, even poisoned and fighting at a disadvantage.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:47.670
Sequioa continued to press the attack with his dagger until Zinnia finally put the ghoul down for good.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:50.870
When the party searched the corpses, they found something unexpected.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.590
A note addressed directly to the four of them.

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:58.950
It was written by a necromancer who called the temple my home and the party interlopers and thieves.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:03.190
He thanked them with cold sarcasm for the harvest of death they had left in their wake.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.789
Every corpse they had created was a resource he intended to use against them.

00:09:07.029 --> 00:09:08.310
The note went on at length.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:17.990
My God, this person's busy, Calmer observed, to specifically mock Calmer as a disgrace, unqualified to be head of the Earth Temple, his approach to the rituals, all wrong.

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:22.870
Calmer read it with an expression of mild defense, then folded it and carefully tucked it away.

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:27.430
Piercing what they knew, Zinnia rolling a 21 and Zephyr a natural 20.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:31.029
The party formed a hypothesis about the threat.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:37.830
They remembered Romag mutter that the undead on the first level no longer reported to him, which implied they had once reported to somebody.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:43.750
Barkinaier had once led the Earth Temple before being promoted to the upper levels, and Romag had taken his place.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:54.470
They suspected another figure conducted to the transition might be the necromancer behind the attacks and might resent the party's occupation of the temple, but his identities and motives remained unconfirmed.

00:09:54.629 --> 00:09:58.550
Whoever he was, the party's trail of bodies had given him more material to work with.

00:09:58.789 --> 00:10:00.550
They would need to find him, and soon.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:08.950
The group's final discovery of the day came in an oddly shaped chamber bisected by a low stone wall and holding back a pool of water, the temple's water supply.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:14.870
Calmly dryly noted that the last time they thought they found a bought water supply, it turned out to be a creature from hell.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:27.750
Zephyr stepped inside to investigate, and rolling a dismal eight on investig on immediately slipped on the algae slick, subtly sloping floor, sliding hard to the far wall.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:35.269
Calmer threw him a rope, and once steadied, Zephyr spotted a large, round, slime-covered object resting at the bottom of the pool.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.710
He tied the rope around himself, took a deep breath, and dove.

00:10:38.789 --> 00:10:43.830
The first attempt failed and nearly dislodged the object entirely, sending it tumbling further into the murk.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:50.150
But on the second dive, Zephyr with a 14 just barely seized it and wrenched it free just before his lungs gave out.

00:10:50.389 --> 00:10:57.830
Zinnia helped Calmer haul him back to the surface, and when the slime was covered away, the object revealed itself to be a finely crafted shield plus one.

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.389
Calmer accepted it with great satisfaction.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.110
Very well done.

00:11:01.269 --> 00:11:02.070
That was very well done.

00:11:02.389 --> 00:11:07.509
And as the party themselves gathered to move on, the Minotaur's earlier words drifted back to them.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:11.910
It had mentioned black-cloaked bandits attacking its territory, and now they understood.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.310
Some of those bandits had not been living at all.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.910
The Terminator, it turned out, could eat the undead, but preferred fresh meat.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.910
As the saying goes, beggars can't be pickers.

